    workflow: ["add validates the Task outcome and its owning Function, parses --every and the 24-hour HH:MM time, validates the IANA timezone, creates a dormant Task, computes the next real instant, and persists the Schedule.", "The process checks due Schedules without making a model or search call.", "At a due time Arturo selects an available qualified staffed Worker and queues the existing Task; the Worker runtime alone changes it from queued to running.", "Later due times queue that same Task only after it completes and reselect an available qualified Worker.", "An unfinished Task makes the due occurrence skip, records its reason, and advances the Schedule by one local day or week, including daylight-saving changes."],
    verification: ["Run /schedule list and /schedule inspect immediately after add.", "Confirm the dormant Task ID, cadence, local time, timezone, owning Function, Enterprise, search query, and next UTC instant.", "After the due time, inspect /timeline and /tasks.", "Confirm that later completed occurrences retain the same Task ID while Worker selection reflects availability.", "For web research, inspect the Task search query and resulting evidence Artefact."],
    failures: ["Use daily or a weekday for --every, exact 24-hour HH:MM syntax, and an IANA timezone such as Pacific/Auckland.", "The Task's Function must belong to the selected Enterprise.", "An unfinished Task skips the current occurrence; a missing qualified staffed AI Worker also produces a recorded skip. The Schedule does not grant backup tools, file access, web access, or other execution authority.", "Web research fails closed when query, Worker authority, provider readiness, policy, or call allowance is missing."],
    boundaries: ["The current scheduler supports daily or weekly local-time recurrence; it is not a full cron-expression or calendar system.", "A scheduled backup still requires a real, authorized backup tool or integration. A language model cannot honestly claim that files were copied without one.", "Scheduling queues a completed Task but does not guarantee successful execution, accurate output, or external delivery.", "Removing a Schedule does not erase the Task, prior occurrences, evidence, or audit records."],
